<title>JAPAN: Nissan to form cellular phone venture.</title>
<headline>Nissan to form cellular phone venture.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nissan Motor Co Ltd said on Monday it would set up a wholly owned subsidiary on Tuesday to strengthen development and research into cellular phone technology.</p>
<p>The new company, Nissan Communication System Ltd, will be set up in Tokyo with capitalisation of 50 million yen, it said. The company will create 14 jobs.</p>
<p>Nissan has capital participation in all nine companies of the Digital Tu-Ka group, a nationwide cellular phone service venture, including a 30 percent stake in Digital Tuka Kansai, it said.</p>
</text>
